1
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:13,340
Try letting go of peace, keeping it light.

2
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:26,860
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa.

3
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:33,980
I kicked a pebble,
and even my shoes flew off.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,240
onto the head of the carpenter
who had me in a choke hold.

5
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:48,460
They laughed at me for still being a brat.

6
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if I somehow deliver
some cheer somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,620
Katsushika, one yawn, nothing changes.

8
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,500
The streetscape is strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,640
From the pointed hat's water jug,

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,780
the sunset falls into the big sky.

11
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:25,260
Tomorrow will end just like this too,
won't it?

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,380
Katsushika Shibamata,
I lost even happiness too.

13
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:33,880
Because I'm the foolish
me who finally noticed.

14
00:02:00,380 --> 00:02:03,539
Honestly, Chin-kichi.
We got made to skip school,

15
00:02:03,589 --> 00:02:06,340
and we were roped into helping
with a donation box theft.

16
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:10,540
Hmph, look who's talking.
You tagged along happily enough.

17
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:11,420
Well, yeah.

18
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,494
Speaking of which, Kankichi-kun.

19
00:02:15,544 --> 00:02:18,780
We got yelled at by the principal for climbing up the Obake Entotsu,
didn't we?

20
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,780
Right, the substitute teacher, Yoko-sensei.

21
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,460
Kankichi's totally head over heels for her.

22
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:26,920
You two were the same way, weren't you?

23
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,540
Thanks, Yoko-sensei.

24
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:32,700
I remember.

25
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,860
Like when we opened the Kachidoki
Bridge after it got stuck, right?

26
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:38,980
Yeah, but that was in middle school.

27
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:42,180
Geez, you only remember the bad stuff.

28
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:44,560
We haven't all seen each other in ages,
you know.

29
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:47,720
Shouldn't we be sharing
more heartwarming memories?

30
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:48,400
Yes.

31
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,120
Oh my.

32
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,880
Our memories with Kankichi are...

33
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:54,420
either getting scolded or made to stand in the hallway.
That's all.

34
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:59,460
You too, you know.

35
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:06,360
But who would've thought the wildest kid in the grade,
Kankichi, would become a police officer?

36
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:09,040
Really,
you never know how the world turns out.

37
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,480
And that honor student Murase...

38
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:19,680
Murase? You mean Kenji Murase,
who transferred away in third year?

39
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:22,140
We often went to the
movie theater too, right?

40
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:25,340
Yeah, what was that
movie theater called again?

41
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:26,680
Hey, Kankichi.

42
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,180
What happened to Ken-chan?

43
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:36,440
Chin-kichi, why are you so quiet?

44
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:40,260
You work for the police and didn't know?

45
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:42,160
So what?

46
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,040
He got arrested.

47
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:49,560
You're joking.
Ken-chan, the smartest one, would never...

48
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:56,020
No way, seriously?

49
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:59,380
It was splashed across the evening paper the day before yesterday,
you know.

50
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:00,720
Why would Ken-chan...

51
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,360
No way...

52
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:05,240
He was a yakuza executive.

53
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:06,260
What?!

54
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,080
Ken-chan?

55
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,520
I'm going home.

56
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,820
I'm skipping the after-party.

57
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:12,280
Hey,

58
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:14,720
Kankichi!

59
00:04:21,380 --> 00:04:25,140
Ryo-chan!

60
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:27,400
Weren't you going to Blasker?

61
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:30,080
Yes. Do you have the evening
paper from the day before yesterday?

62
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,420
Old newspapers are by the sink.

63
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,480
Ken-chan

64
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:51,200
What's going on with
Murase of the Shuneikai?

65
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:52,000
Why?

66
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,520
Ryotsu!

67
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:57,300
Chief, it says he was arrested
right here at our station.

68
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:59,660
Ken... no, Murase is now...

69
00:05:00,080 --> 00:05:04,220
He'll probably be transferred to
Asakusa soon to handle the case.

70
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:06,640
Ryotsu

71
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,300
I wonder what he's doing, senpai.

72
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:11,180
He's not acting like himself.

73
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,160
Clack!

74
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:47,680
Click!

75
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:04,740
What's wrong? Let's go.

76
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,040
Ken-chan

77
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:12,860
Ken-chan, why?

78
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:14,160
Who cares about you!

79
00:06:14,740 --> 00:06:15,800
I don't know you!

80
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:18,180
Hey, stop it!

81
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,660
Are you okay, Ryotsu?

82
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:23,260
Come on, get in.

83
00:06:25,280 --> 00:06:26,020
Ken-chan!

84
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:31,160
Wait!

85
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,360
Ken-chan!

86
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:11,580
Here you go, Ryo-chan.

87
00:07:12,280 --> 00:07:15,760
I can't believe Murase was your senpai's
best friend from elementary school.

88
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,800
That poor guy.

89
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,200
I heard it from the
detective who interrogated him.

90
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:23,200
Even though he took the lead in
negotiations with the Odaeba-gumi,

91
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,340
instead of hiding him, the group

92
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:27,420
reportedly informed on his hideout.

93
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:31,680
Yakuza these days don't have the old-fashioned sense of honor and humanity,
do they?

94
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:34,360
Ryotsu.

95
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:37,400
They may have been best friends,
but a yakuza is still a yakuza.

96
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,780
We live in different worlds.

97
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:45,160
Yeah, treating Ryo-chan like he's beneath him,
they're not friends at all.

98
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,500
He wasn't like that before.

99
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:52,360
He was a rich kid,
and the smartest in the class,

100
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:54,160
and he really hit it off with Myō.

101
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:56,420
When was it again? That guy...

102
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,960
got scolded by his strict,
elite bureaucrat father,

103
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:02,400
and once ran away from home to our place.

104
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:04,700
Kankichi!

105
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,160
Hey, you're still an Edokko, aren't you?

106
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,580
You've got to go for it,
charging straight in head-first.

107
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,120
Ahh, that's good.

108
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,000
This is it, this is it.

109
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:18,060
Alright, then I'll have some too.

110
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,000
Wheee, seriously...

111
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:25,280
Idiot, who copies someone
even when it comes to drinking?

112
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:29,040
Everything's starting to spin.

113
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:32,040
Right in front of us,
there's a brat, seriously.

114
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:34,640
It's you, giving alcohol to a kid.

115
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,700
I didn't really make him drink it.

116
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:38,040
It's the same thing.

117
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,520
Mom wins!

118
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:43,820
He's pretending to be drunk, the little...

119
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,820
Dad!

120
00:08:46,820 --> 00:08:49,480
Stop it, we're eating, you know!

121
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:55,520
What's wrong, Ken-chan?
Didn't you like the food?

122
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:58,980
I envy your mom.

123
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:02,938
Me? You're kidding.
Living in that huge house,

124
00:09:02,988 --> 00:09:05,000
having a car drive you everywhere,

125
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:08,840
while my place is like this,
and my dad's a brute,

126
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:12,620
and my mom just walked out.
You're much better off, Ken-chan.

127
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:15,826
No. A fun family meal like this,

128
00:09:15,876 --> 00:09:18,360
I've never once had one.

129
00:09:18,360 --> 00:09:20,020
Why's that?

130
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:22,020
Never mind that.

131
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:25,960
Anyway, Kenbō, if you ever feel lonely,
come eat at our place anytime.

132
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:27,280
Is that really all right?

133
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:31,140
We don't have fancy food,
but you're always welcome, Ken-chan.

134
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:32,580
Thank you, auntie.

135
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:34,840
Uncle, like this, right?

136
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,220
Good eating! I like you.

137
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,540
Well, have a drink.

138
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:41,620
You there.

139
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:43,040
Oops.

140
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:52,800
He was a good guy who understood
the warmth of the old town.

141
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,140
Yes, this is Kameari Park police box.

142
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:35,460
What? Murase escaped?

143
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:37,120
Nakagawa, take over.

144
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:39,020
This is Ohara.

145
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:41,560
Yes, understood.

146
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:44,880
We've received a request from Katsushika
Station for investigative cooperation.

147
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:45,960
Nakagawa, let's go.

148
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:46,240
Yes.

149
00:10:47,260 --> 00:10:48,240
I'm coming too.

150
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:50,500
You're off duty. You don't have to come.

151
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:51,380
I'm going.

152
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:54,000
You may have to put cuffs on your friend,
you know.

153
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:56,180
I'm a police officer.

154
00:10:58,620 --> 00:10:59,120
Ryotsu

155
00:10:59,120 --> 00:11:02,520
Got it, change into your uniforms.

156
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:03,000
Yes.

157
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:08,080
Murase wants revenge on the
Shūikai for betraying him,

158
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:10,060
so he most likely fled.

159
00:11:10,060 --> 00:11:14,720
Lock down Asakusa 9-chome, where the Shūikai is based,
and the surrounding area thoroughly.

160
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,840
We've arrived from Katsushika
Station with thirty officers as backup.

161
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,120
Good work.

162
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:22,100
The suspect took a gun and is on the run.

163
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:23,600
Be very careful.

164
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:26,140
So, what leads do we have on Murase?

165
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:29,020
He'll probably show up here,
at the Shūikai's location.

166
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,180
We have no trace of his whereabouts at all.

167
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:35,140
Over there!

168
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:37,420
Senpai.

169
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:49,240
I know Asakusa well from Urajima, so.

170
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:50,380
Shall we take a look?

171
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:52,840
Just wait for the investigation
to uncover the truth.

172
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:11,640
Notes

173
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:16,300
So you do remember me after all.

174
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:17,380
Ken-chan

175
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:19,880
Shut up! Don't come near me!

176
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:23,960
Ken-chan, we used to play tag
around here all the time, didn't we?

177
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:27,820
Can't you hear me?
If you come any closer, I'll shoot!

178
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:32,060
Pistol play Brings back memories.

179
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:33,600
Come on, then!

180
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:36,740
You'll pay for this, I'm going to shoot!

181
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:43,940
The sound of a gunshot!

182
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:44,640
What?

183
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:45,720
Over there!

184
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,800
Hurry, Nakagawa! It has to be Murase!

185
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:01,480
Not bad! Playing wrestling now, are we?

186
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:02,860
Don't mess with me!

187
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:10,340
That was a good punch.

188
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:12,600
You really intend to get in my way?

189
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:14,440
Of course.

190
00:13:22,300 --> 00:13:23,340
Damn it.

191
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:27,920
Surrender, Ken-chan.

192
00:13:28,540 --> 00:13:30,100
I don't know what happened,

193
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:32,720
but the moment you gave up on your life,
you lost.

194
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:34,120
Shut up!

195
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:37,340
You big idiot.

196
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,320
You're still tough in a fight, as always.

197
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:52,280
Well, yeah.

198
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:57,380
Chief, let's arrest him.

199
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:58,400
Wait.

200
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:01,260
Let's leave it to him.

201
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:09,880
Ken-chan,
why on earth did you become a yakuza?

202
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:30,853
In middle school,

203
00:14:30,903 --> 00:14:34,440
my dad and Mom divorcing
was where my bad luck began.

204
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:38,680
I wanted to go with Mom,
but Dad wouldn't let go of me.

205
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:43,380
Then, in my third year, Dad got thrown
in the slammer over a corruption scandal.

206
00:14:44,660 --> 00:14:47,191
It was a famous private junior high,

207
00:14:47,241 --> 00:14:50,340
but because of my dad,
I got bullied horribly.

208
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:55,600
I couldn't take it anymore, so I sent the bully
to the hospital and ended up in juvenile detention.

209
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:58,940
A downward spiral of a life,
just like I described before.

210
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:05,080
Before I knew it, I was living on this street.
Don't be such a spoiled brat.

211
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:09,560
Don't blame other people for your own life!

212
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:18,180
You have to carve out your own life.
Have you forgotten about Yone-san?

213
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:19,820
Kome-goma...

214
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:22,440
So many of them...

215
00:15:22,440 --> 00:15:23,900
Lucky you.

216
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:25,920
Kan-chan, give me one.

217
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:26,980
No, no.

218
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:30,400
This kome-goma is my treasure.
I won it in a match.

219
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,480
If you want one, Ken-chan,
you'll get good at it too.

220
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:35,240
But I'm bad at kome-goma.

221
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,480
I'll make it worth your while.

222
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:38,660
Really?

223
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:43,760
No.

224
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:46,640
You have to put more
energy into spinning it.

225
00:15:46,640 --> 00:15:47,260
One more time.

226
00:15:48,680 --> 00:15:49,040
Yeah.

227
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:04,420
That's right, spirit!
Spirit, spirit, spirit!

228
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:08,640
Listen,
no hard feelings after the match, got it?

229
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:10,920
Of course.

230
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:12,940
Go for it, Esuke!

231
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:16,800
Go!

232
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,780
Ten-chan wins!

233
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,000
Yes!

234
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:27,200
How about that?

235
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:29,640
This guy's got no strength, but he's tough!

236
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:31,380
Damn it! You'll pay for this!

237
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,000
Beeter! I'll take you on anytime!

238
00:16:35,360 --> 00:16:38,780
Look, Kan-chan! I've won so many rice-goma!

239
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,900
One, two, three!

240
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:42,640
Yeah, that's amazing!

241
00:16:43,420 --> 00:16:46,720
Ken-chan's is a special rice-goma
made by squashing a big one.

242
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,800
Plus he's left-handed, so he'll never lose!

243
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:51,420
-Really?
-Yeah!

244
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:53,620
Exactly 100!

245
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:56,160
What, 100? That's more than me!

246
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,820
Amazing,
it all started with just this one rice-goma.

247
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:02,900
Nobody in the neighborhood
can beat Ken-chan anymore.

248
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:05,340
Let's go on a trip to
the next town tomorrow.

249
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:06,060
Yeah.

250
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:10,722
That smile you had when you
won it with your own strength,

251
00:17:10,772 --> 00:17:11,700
was the best.

252
00:17:12,480 --> 00:17:14,460
Right, that happened too.

253
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:17,660
Do you remember where
that rice-goma ended up?

254
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:18,440
Nope.

255
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:20,880
I still remember it.

256
00:17:21,580 --> 00:17:24,900
It was the day before
Ken-chan moved to Shibuya.

257
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,840
I'm giving you the rice-goma we won,
Kan-chan.

258
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,540
Really?

259
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:36,720
I have to go to cram school to get into a private junior high,
so I won't be able to play anymore.

260
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:38,840
And I collected a hundred of them, too.

261
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:42,280
This rice-goma is a
badge of honor for a man.

262
00:17:43,580 --> 00:17:46,480
Yeah, but if they find out,
they'll throw them away.

263
00:17:47,420 --> 00:17:48,920
I've got an idea.

264
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:54,000
Let's bury them under
this tree as our treasure.

265
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:58,300
That way we can dig them up
whenever we want to use them.

266
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,360
I see. You're smart, Kan-chan.

267
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:03,320
Big brother, it's this one.

268
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:07,360
Hey, I hear you took rice-goma
from my little brother.

269
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:09,880
I didn't take it,
I won it fair and square in a match.

270
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:12,340
Shut up. That's the one. Hand it over.

271
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:14,280
It hurts.

272
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:16,160
Hey, stop it! Let go of me!

273
00:18:17,460 --> 00:18:19,140
You little brat.

274
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:20,000
Kan-chan!

275
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,700
Sorry for being a brat,
you big lug, Usudoro.

276
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:23,300
What did you say?

277
00:18:27,100 --> 00:18:27,820
Big brother.

278
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:31,980
Come back another day, punk.

279
00:18:31,980 --> 00:18:34,160
You're really strong, Kan-chan.

280
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:36,000
Beating up sixth graders like that.

281
00:18:36,980 --> 00:18:38,400
I never lose a fight.

282
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:40,900
If Kan-chan uses that strength

283
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,320
and turns into a bad guy,

284
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,920
I'll become a lawyer and save him,
I promise.

285
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:47,820
That's harsh, Ken-chan.

286
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:54,020
And I said that, but I ended up a yakuza.

287
00:18:54,380 --> 00:18:56,300
And you became a cop.

288
00:18:57,020 --> 00:18:59,920
Life really doesn't go the way you want,
does it.

289
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:01,300
Kan-chan.

290
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,760
You're saying whatever you like, aren't you.

291
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:07,580
I'm the Prime Minister, you know.

292
00:19:08,780 --> 00:19:09,660
You bet.

293
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:12,280
Storming in there doesn't matter anymore.

294
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:15,000
I'll turn myself in,
like you said, Kan-chan.

295
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:16,780
I see.

296
00:19:17,820 --> 00:19:19,140
You've got a top-notch brain.

297
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:21,040
You can restart as many times as you like.

298
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,700
Though we got off to a pretty late start.

299
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:26,160
Hey, the police station's that way.

300
00:19:27,180 --> 00:19:28,100
I know.

301
00:19:28,820 --> 00:19:30,340
There's somewhere I want to stop by.

302
00:19:30,780 --> 00:19:33,420
I'll definitely turn
myself in before sunset.

303
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:34,880
Will you let me go?

304
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:35,720
Kan-chan.

305
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:39,120
You finally called me by my old name again.

306
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:40,580
Got it.

307
00:19:41,840 --> 00:19:42,200
Thanks.

308
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:45,440
I'll be waiting for you at the station.

309
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:49,040
Senpai

310
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:51,300
Nakagawa

311
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:53,260
Senpai,
are you sure it's okay to let him go?

312
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:54,900
Why aren't you arresting him?

313
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:56,660
He says he'll turn himself in.

314
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:58,620
You actually believed him?

315
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:00,820
It's all right, Nakagawa.

316
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:01,780
Chief

317
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:02,760
Ryotsu

318
00:20:02,760 --> 00:20:06,760
You've closed the distance that opened up over those thirty years,
haven't you?

319
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:07,640
Yes.

320
00:20:18,940 --> 00:20:20,920
Senpai, sunset is almost here.

321
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:22,160
Senpai.

322
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,600
You're such a nag.

323
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:24,640
Don't worry.

324
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:26,300
He said he'll turn himself in properly.

325
00:20:26,940 --> 00:20:27,600
But -

326
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:28,840
Are you an idiot?

327
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,820
After getting the gun back,

328
00:20:30,820 --> 00:20:32,360
why didn't you arrest him?

329
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:33,940
He's a yakuza.

330
00:20:33,940 --> 00:20:35,860
If Murase doesn't turn himself in,

331
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:38,820
you'll be held fully responsible.

332
00:20:39,260 --> 00:20:39,980
Understood.

333
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:41,480
Wait.

334
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:43,757
Ryotsu, it's fine.

335
00:20:43,807 --> 00:20:46,380
You just need to trust Murase.

336
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:47,560
But...

337
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:50,900
Thanks to you, I'm well practiced
at writing resignation letters.

338
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,100
Chief...

339
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:58,820
The sun has set.

340
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:01,720
Looks like I'll have
to write my resignation.

341
00:21:02,460 --> 00:21:04,340
No, Ken-chan will definitely come.

342
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:11,260
Ohara, you were supposed to be watching him,
and look what you've done!

343
00:21:11,260 --> 00:21:15,500
I trusted you and put you in charge of the reinforcements,
and now you're telling me my face is completely ruined?

344
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:16,940
I'm sorry.

345
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:20,100
Why, why didn't you come back, Ken-chan?

346
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:23,320
Anyway, I'll bow my head with you.

347
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:26,180
Let's go apologize to the
chief of Asakusa Police Station.

348
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:27,860
Senpai, look here.

349
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,420
Ken-chan.

350
00:21:44,860 --> 00:21:47,720
You're late! You had us worried sick.

351
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:52,800
Sorry, it's been thirty years,
so I took a wrong turn.

352
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,000
Kan-chan.

353
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:02,760
You idiot, do you think I'd put
handcuffs on someone who turned himself in?

354
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:04,200
Come on, let's go.

355
00:22:05,880 --> 00:22:06,500
Chief.

356
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:19,880
I'm sure it was around here.

357
00:22:24,940 --> 00:22:26,240
The ground's been dug up.

358
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:32,020
Found it.

359
00:22:36,940 --> 00:22:37,500
A letter.

360
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:41,880
Kan-chan has sharp instincts, after all.

361
00:22:42,560 --> 00:22:44,720
Kan-chan will probably
come to this spot too.

362
00:22:46,060 --> 00:22:47,600
Thanks to meeting Kan-chan,

363
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:50,460
I've got back the heart
I had thirty years ago.

364
00:22:51,180 --> 00:22:54,480
After thirty years,
I'll borrow the rice-goma for a while.

365
00:22:56,200 --> 00:22:57,400
Because this is my pride.

366
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:01,140
It may be impossible a second time, but

367
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:04,240
Next time we meet,
I'll definitely be back on my feet.

368
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,920
I'm looking forward to that time.

369
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:08,120
Ken-chan...

370
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:09,860
That kid...

371
00:23:12,520 --> 00:23:15,680
Let's open this treasure together
when it's the 21st century.

372
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:19,460
Yeah, I wonder what Kan-chan
will be in the 21st century.

373
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:21,320
Prime minister, of course!

374
00:23:21,760 --> 00:23:24,740
Ken-chan's smart,
so he'll definitely be a lawyer.

375
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:28,680
Yeah, Kan-chan,
don't forget me even after I move, okay?

376
00:23:29,160 --> 00:23:31,000
We'll be friends for life.

377
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:34,580
Of course, I'd never forget you.

378
00:23:36,580 --> 00:23:39,940
I'm looking forward to meeting
here again on New Year's Day 2001.

379
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:43,020
Okay, let's bury it
deeper so nobody finds it.

380
00:23:47,420 --> 00:23:50,420
Well, since I've come
all the way to Asakusa...

381
00:23:50,420 --> 00:23:52,540
Maybe I'll stop by and see my old man.

382
00:24:15,620 --> 00:24:23,620
Surprise and commotion,
spirit and resolution, swift and vanished,

383
00:24:23,620 --> 00:24:35,280
decided and inspired and bouncing,
gathered and in action, flying away.

384
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:40,020
Above all, the amazing power!

385
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:52,260
Everyone gather, if you come here,
the dreamlike final energy.

386
00:24:53,360 --> 00:25:03,400
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, drawing the universe,
standing on the ground, the star of Kameari spins around in a circle.

387
00:25:05,520 --> 00:25:08,540
"That'll do, right?" "Like hell it will!"

388
00:25:31,940 --> 00:25:37,200
Next time on

389
00:25:42,260 --> 00:25:43,660
Thank you for watching.

